    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Labrador Park hosts Singapore’s only publicly accessible rocky sea‑cliff, a remnant of the island’s original coastline.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Labrador_Nature_Reserve"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Dragon’s Teeth Gate, a replica of a 19th‑century landmark, marks the entrance to Keppel Harbour.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://singaporetripguide.com/destinations/historical-landmarks-and-sightseeing-around-labrador-park"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 2002, 10 hectares of coastal vegetation and rocky shore were gazetted as a nature reserve, safeguarding local biodiversity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
